    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_3208be341dd92479ab39593fd2307b8bb0875500060dafead28aa4b0f379db7c",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Under the paper's RH assumption, the introduction organizes prime-number-theorem remainder information by mode of control: a baseline pointwise estimate, a sharper estimate outside a set of finite logarithmic measure, two mean-value claims, and an almost-all consequence of the mean-square claim (3). The source further says that the finite-logarithmic-measure proof combines the arguments for (1) and (3), but it does not disclose that combination here. Thus the useful structure is a hierarchy and dependency map among pointwise, averaged, almost-all, and exceptional-set conclusions, not a formula-level theorem reconstruction.",
