    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_a28e94adf9e9c1b085d0312cecf5fc80b8b37189325c4a72df32247f64d33f40",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The paper specializes the earlier formulas (6) and (7) at a fixed parameter to obtain the local integral estimate (8), then says that an unspecified splitting-up argument aggregates it into the announced mean-square estimate (3). The substantive move is therefore local-to-global reuse of an already established estimate; the bookkeeping that makes the aggregation valid remains a proof burden in this compressed span.",
