    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_e80faf6fe0dcfe4f00383e15dbcc7e39653ef9c7b0c4aa46501064e5293e2c70",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Under the paper's RH setup, the explicit formula changes the prime-counting remainder into a truncated sum over complex zeta zeros plus an unreadable error term. Splitting the zero ordinates at log X makes the low range directly manageable: aggregating the stated logarithmic bound on the number of zeros in each unit-height interval gives the source's qualitative target-scale bound for ordinates below log X. The complementary range is left unresolved in this span.",
