    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6c8ab95f90f9a3f9d415b3651492dabd65f7cf2b423f5674b3a0f9c7a645959d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source distinguishes several levels of usable zero information. Truncated zero sums plus mean-square estimates support exceptional-set and averaged short-interval conclusions, while finer data enter in different roles: multiplicities survive the fixed-cutoff diagonal calculation and determine the leading global mean-value contribution, whereas pair-density is reported as an additional correlation hypothesis that strengthens a pointwise remainder estimate.",
