      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The exceptional-set and short-interval arguments reuse a common architecture: an explicit-formula representation is cut at an adjustable zero-height scale, componentwise mean-square control is converted into the target form, and the cutoff is then calibrated differently—toward summable logarithmic bad-set measure on exponential blocks in the first argument and toward a lower-order integrated short-interval discrepancy in the second.",
